    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "French Estates are delighted to present No. 809 Ladycastle to the market. This beautifully positioned large duplex overlooks the 18th green of the iconic Arnold Palmer designed inland links, K Club South Golf Course, in one of Ireland's most exclusive and desirable gated community developments located on the 550 acre estate. 809 Ladycastle is nestled in Block A and is immaculately presented and styled with well appointed, spacious and light filled living accommodation and two en-suite double bedrooms on the second floor. This idyllic and peaceful setting with panoramic views of the undulating dunes and the dramatic landscape of the Palmer South Golf Course at The K Club ensures breathtaking beauty and absolute tranquility pervade every inch of your surrounds. The quaint village of Straffan is only a short stroll away and with the N7 and M4 close by, you will be in Dublin City in about 40 minutes. This exquisite home affords the discerning buyer a tranquil lifestyle in a peaceful and beautiful country setting while\nclose proximity to major transport routes, Dublin City and Airport make this the ideal location.\n\nAccommodation\n\nEntrance Hall / Landing: 5.18 m x 3.71 m with marble tiles, brushed chrome sockets, alarm panel, i lighting with recessed spot lights and a feature wrap around staircase.\n\nLounge / Dining Area 8.87 m x 5.20 m Spacious and light filled with French doors providing access to the large private south west facing full length balcony with panoramic views of the dramatic landscape overlooking the 18th Green on the Palmer South Golf Course at The K Club. This luxurious room has a solid oak wood floor, a belle cheminee marble fireplace with a gas fire inset and recessed lighting.\n\nKitchen 2.94 m x 4.184 m A stylish designer kitchen with high gloss finish, marble worktops, Gaggenau appliances, recessed spot lights and a marble tiled floor.\n\nOffice / Study 3.07 m x 3.57 m On the first floor with an oak wood floor, recessed lighting, overlooking the front entrance.\n\nGuest WC: 2.14 m x 1.76 m Partially tiled with a marble floor, wc, whb, recessed spot lights and Villeroy and Boch sanitary wear.\n\nSecond Floor\nMaster Bedroom: 4.17 m x 5.79 m with large walk in wardrobes, recessed spot lights, carpet flooring and French doors providing access to the balcony. The balcony provides spectacular views of the Palmer South golf course.\nEn-suite: 2.60 m x 3.41 m Partially tiled with a marble tiled floor, wc, whc, Jacuzzi bath, hansgrohe shower cubicle, recessed spot lights and Villeroy and Boch sanitary wear.\n\nBedroom 2: 5.19 m x 3.502 m with built in wardrobes, recessed spot lights, carpet flooring and French doors providing access to the balcony.\nEn-suite: 1.56 m x 2.83 m Partially tiled with a marble floor, wc, whband shower cubicle.\n\nOutside\n\nThe high level finishes continue outside with professionally landscaped grounds and manicured cobblelock pathways surrounding this idyllic residence.\n\nFixtures and Fittings\nIncluded in the sale is all carpets, curtains, blinds, light fittings and integrated units. \n\nTenure\nLong Leasehold.\n\nServices\nGas fired heating, mains water, drainage and electricity.\n\nService Charges and Membership\nFor 2026 the service charges are 5,180. In Ladycastle at the K Club, please note, there are 2 mandatory memberships of the entire resort (both golf courses North & South, gym, spa, swimming pool, fishing and discounted hotel services) that come with all properties there. They are activated to approved buyers when the sale closes. The annual dues that apply are 7,250 for one party and 3,750 for the other party. They are mandatory as long as you own the property, once you sell the property they transfer to the new owner on completion. This is a condition of the planning permission.\n\nDirections\nComing from Dublin on the M4, take the exit 7 for Maynooth. At Maynooth Business Campus roundabout, take the 2nd exit onto Straffan Rd. Proceed past Barberstown Castle towards Straffan Village passing past both Churches. You will pass the main entrance to the K Club.\n\nFeatures \n- c. 171 sq. m\n- Mood lighting\n- Built in 2006\n- Interior designed to a high specification with Villeroy and Boch\n sanitary ware\n- High level of security\n- South west facing balconies\n- Alarmed\n- Gas fired central heating with gas effect fire\n- Fitted hand crafted wardrobes in the bedrooms\n\n "
      },
